{"ts": "2026-11-07T00:28:43.658430Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0028Z-c1f6", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-061daa6c", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied as its scenario is written. The tracing test passed and asserts every clause of the scenario: an empty factory log before the first run, one call after five sequential runs with the worker-entry href and the default env and resourceLimits, size 2 and respawns 0; twelve concurrent runs on a size 2 pool giving one distinct value with two factory calls; a size 1 pool finishing BUSY then 1 to 5 in order; the size 3 pool spawning with stackSizeMb 8 and maxOldGenerationSizeMb 256; every BAD_OPTIONS row of the test plan throwing a synchronous SandboxError with the listed code, option and message, including the opts rows, the unknown-key ordering rows with zero getter reads and the two unreadable rows; size winning over graceMs; and every GOOD_OPTIONS row accepted with the counting getter read once. The judge called the test inadequate only because it omits a Proxy whose getPrototypeOf trap throws, which no BAD_OPTIONS row lists; that gap is a code defect against the requirement text and is handled by the finding F-44115141, which is rejected separately, not a failure of this scenario.", "text_sha256": "fbc3659b99dbcea9d5a8248951bd078eceb471606ec9be04673e4f88a1607e54", "answer_sha256": "a71d1bbf2111eed3a7d05da726e177ba70d99a034f949697793312f3fd7ccbdf", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T00:28:43.660405Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0028Z-c1f6", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-005", "target": "F-44115141", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is correct and is not waived. The requirement says createWorkerSandbox throws SandboxError SANDBOX_INVALID with option opts for a getter or Proxy trap that throws. In pool.ts the plain-object check isPlainObject runs on the raw argument before either try/catch of readPoolOptions, and it calls Object.getPrototypeOf on the value, which invokes a Proxy's getPrototypeOf trap. A Proxy whose getPrototypeOf trap throws therefore leaks its raw error out of createWorkerSandbox instead of the typed SandboxError. The fix is in production code only: the prototype check must be inside the same protected path that already turns a throwing ownKeys trap or getter into the opts could not be read error. WHEN createWorkerSandbox receives an opts value that is a Proxy whose getPrototypeOf trap throws THEN it throws synchronously a SandboxError with code SANDBOX_INVALID, message opts could not be read and details option opts, and no other error escapes.", "text_sha256": "028cfac427b3923e556553cf751c6d4a91dc2eeaa58e4d48d961eaf855f62509", "answer_sha256": "346e56d602095c7f948c432ab50aab7353f2e2d965fdaa9175e87e3a9c09d108", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
